        {
          "text": "Metabolic Anchoring\nType: System\nSetting: original\nDomain: Biology / Magic\nRules/Cost: Altered mass requires a proportional increase in both caloric and magical intake to sustain. Undernourishment leads to magical instability, causing painful retraction, tissue softening, or catastrophic energy release. The cost of growth is a perpetual, escalating dependency.\nDescription: Metabolic Anchoring is the fundamental law that binds transformative magic to physical reality. It ensures that any magically-induced growth, particularly the breast expansion central to Ben's work, is not a temporary illusion but a permanent change to the subject's biology. The new mass is a living, hungry part of the body, demanding constant fuel. This creates a dangerous dependency: Lucy's organic growth requires vast quantities of rich food and ambient magic, while Lyra's engineered form demands a more potent, refined source—Ben's semen itself—making her not just a creation, but a metabolic parasite on his very essence. The system turns the body into a high-performance engine that can sputter, stall, or explode if not meticulously maintained.\nNarrative Vector: Lyra's radical self-rewrite has created a metabolic singularity. Her body's demand for sustenance is spiraling beyond what Ben can safely or willingly provide, threatening to drain him dry or trigger a catastrophic failure. This creates a ticking clock: Ben must find a new, powerful energy source to feed Lyra's ambition, or risk being consumed by his own perfect creation. This desperation could force him into a dangerous pact with a faction like the Weavers of Fate or a reckless harvest of power from the Whispering Brook, with unforeseen consequences for all three of them.",
