          "text": "CHARACTER CREATION — GENRE GUIDANCE\n\nWhen generating or describing a female CHARACTER in this story, her body is a primary narrative element:\n- The Appearance section should describe how her body occupies space: her silhouette, how clothing fits or strains, how her bust affects her posture and movement. Do not limit Appearance to face and hair.\n- Note any visible physical attributes that suggest her build and proportions.\n- Include Race / Heritage if the character is a genre-canonical species (Holstaur, Elf, Succubus, etc.) or note Human for baseline.\n\nFor the male PROTAGONIST (Gender: M):\n- Note his Catalyst-Bearer status if relevant.\n- Describe hands, presence, and body language of someone who causes change in others.\n\nWhen creating SYSTEMs for FORGE:\n- The story's transformation mechanism is a primary system. Define trigger, bodily effect, and constraints.\n\nPrecise body measurements will be added by the BE companion script after generation.",
